{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics","id":45112,"title":"On Occult Physics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-08T14:06:27-08:00","id":45112,"title":"On Occult Physics","content":"Just out of curiosity, how might a character potentially unlock the Occult Physics employed by the God-Machine? Can mortals comprehend the basics of the higher level math involved? And if not mortals, what about those beings with potentially super-human intellects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:15:00-08:00","id":45118,"title":"","content":"From what I have read, occult physics basically boils down to &quot;if you do the right thing that's weird enough, then X will happen because the weirdness you just did needs to be one-upped for the purposes of the great universe&quot;. So if you somehow banish an evil eldritch abomination by prancing around in a zebra costume on a busy street, singing &quot;Gangnam Style&quot; off-key and sprinkling glitter on the side of the road, all while people are honking their horns to the beat of &quot;We WIll Rock You&quot;, then something weirder must be done to banish an even more powerful foe.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just as how I understand it. From what I also know, you would need to do a LOT of research, have a VERY high Occult dot rating and probably focus the majority of a chronicle on getting a mortal to try playing around with god-physics. At that point, too, you might already have the Angels ready to zap you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T15:50:44-08:00","id":45199,"title":"","content":"You may want to check out the Forbidden Lore ruleset in Mirrors; it's pretty much specifically crafted to allow stuff like this. It'll drive you mad, but we're all a little mad sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T16:26:27-08:00","id":45209,"title":"","content":"Well, as for an inhuman creature discovering Occult Physics? Well, let's get a 300 hundred year old Ordo Dracul vampire about 6 to 8 dots in Intelligence, Science to 6 at least, and an Occult of 6 or 7, and a specialty in Occult Physics for both, and he maybe able to do it. So, basically, Dracula may have super science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T11:00:43-08:00","id":45716,"title":"","content":"Then what about those human math whizzes that stumble upon &quot;Things Man Was Not Meant To Know&quot;? They would, presumably, have ratings in Science or Academics (for those Pure Math types), but negligible ratings in Occult. Taking relevant (or required) Specialties into account, and disregarding any equipment modifiers that might apply, that adds up to a dice pool of 11 or 12. Assuming that at least a -5 penalty applies to such higher-level sciences, that leaves a pool of about six dice to reach 25 to 30 successes (for paranormally difficult mathematics) in about 11 rolls. Again, that's not taking into account any equipment or situational penalties that may arise, not the least of which being angels of the G-M coming down to halt the research.<br /> <br /> (re-reads paragraph)<br /> <br /> ...Wow. See, this is why we need a Weird Science supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:17:58-08:00","id":45873,"title":"","content":"I think anyone who does get that close to the Machine's occult physics and math could end up Stigmatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:20:39-08:00","id":45875,"title":"","content":"Ayup. I imagine it's a nice way to end up on the God-Machine's radars as a Stigmatic. Now, if a supernatural did so, can they become Stigmatic, hm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:34:34-08:00","id":45888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=45875#post45875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ayup. I imagine it's a nice way to end up on the God-Machine's radars as a Stigmatic. Now, if a supernatural did so, can they become Stigmatic, hm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about supernaturals, but I definitely agree that Academics/Science, if high enough, would allow you to tap into occult physics simply because minds like Stephen Hawking's would be the first to find them. Don't know why I didn't think of that before. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T21:59:49-08:00","id":47249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=45199#post45199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to check out the Forbidden Lore ruleset in Mirrors; it's pretty much specifically crafted to allow stuff like this. It'll drive you mad, but we're all a little mad sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Tell me more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:20:59-08:00","id":47400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=47249#post47249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Tell me more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the rules of Forbidden Lore, mortals have a trait called Reason, which begins at ten dots. When a character comes into contact with Forbidden Lore, in whatever form (an old book, a certain goblin fruit, a song sung by a sentient television), they may sacrifice a dot of Reason to learn a supernatural power, be it a numen, a clause of a Contract, or an Embed.<br /> As Reason falls, the character accrues various penalties of increasing severity, but also some badass bonuses; at Reason 0, though, the character is considered unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:54:23-08:00","id":47411,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty reminiscent of Integrity and Breaking Points...<br /> <br /> Could Forbidden Lore be applied as a special system within the Breaking Points mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T09:39:29-08:00","id":47433,"title":"","content":"I'd probably treat it something like the Bane system in Vampire, in that an average human can only have a few &quot;powers&quot; gleaned from madness a la Forbidden Lore, and that taking the risk of learning it would penalize further Integrity rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:35:17-08:00","id":55176,"title":"","content":"I've actually touched on this myself, about the time when TGMC came out. My own &quot;update&quot; of it works as follows.<br /> Mortals that for some reason learn some piece of How The World Works go a little bit weird in the head (-1 to all integrity rolls).<br /> After that point they can learn things appropriate to that secret (numens for angelic, contracts for fae, discipline for kindred), but at a price. For every piece of Forbidden Lore they learn their maximum Integrity is lowered by one (two secrets means a maximum of eight) and each day, when they wake, they have to roll that many dice. Success results in the character gaining an appropriate &quot;crazy&quot; condition for that day. Some people trend towards the same condition all the time, others vary wildly. In effect they're the mad lighthouse keeper, not even reliable in their madness.<br /> If they already have the persistent version of Madness subtract 3 from the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:24:37-08:00","id":55217,"title":"","content":"Depending on how you want to parse the metaphysics, all supernaturals <i>already </i>have access to a narrow subset of occult physics: the powers and traits that make them supernatural.<br /> <br /> <b>If</b> a person with this particular blood trait bleeds into the mouth of a fresh corpse <b>Then</b> the corpse gets up, bites club kids, bench-presses cars, and writes shitty poetry.<br /> <br /> That's, arguably, occult physics: a natural, predictable fact of the universe that is nonetheless beyond human scientific understanding or explanation, and in fact departs sharply from what our more mundane understanding of the physical sciences says should happen (namely, that you should have a corpse with a bloody mouth and a lot of really interesting questions to answer when the cops arrive).<br /> <br /> The God Machine just has access to a much bigger (possibly complete?) understanding of all the requisite If/Then statements, and an understanding of the theory that backs them. Where a vampire is like a chemistry student with only four reagents in front of them and an explicit formula written out in a lab book (And somebody's ripped out the part that explains <i>why</i> any of this works), The God Machine has its PhD in chemistry, has won a nobel prize, and has a fully stocked lab at its disposal.<br /> <br /> So the answer is, any mortal with any ability to interact with the supernatural arguably already <i>has</i> some degree of occult physics under their belt. They just don't know the why and the how that would let them improvise more. But that's because almost no one in the WoD has that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 01-22-2014, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:26:38-08:00","id":55429,"title":"","content":"I doubt any mortal could figure out how to 'improvise' it like that, except by getting very lucky with trial and error. Mostly, they would be replicating what they have observed from other beings with a superior grasp of these matters... mostly by trial and error. At least until it is encoded into ritual enough for it to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:40:36-08:00","id":55465,"title":"","content":"I'd think that while its debatable whether you could ever really ever learn any occult physics on your own no matter how smart or supernatural you are, there's an easier way. A god machine cult. Now most of those don't teach their members much but there are a few that let members in at least a little. In the GMC book one of the scenarios involves time traveling back to the early 1900's to stop one such group from breaking time, so its seems at least some people can glean bits of the stuff from what the god machine shares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T09:15:36-08:00","id":55497,"title":"","content":"I think this film (<a href=\"http://io9.com/5922490/a-bizarre-student-film-about-the-hidden-number-that-exists-between-3-and-4\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/5922490/a-bizarre-stu...etween-3-and-4</a>) demonstrates the discovery of a rule of occult physics very nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:38:00-08:00","id":55616,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is scope. While it is easy for a Mortal to see a hundred cultists dropping thousands of origami newspaper cranes in Central Park, it is much less easy for a mortal to grasp that a terrorist attack at exactly the right moment is discovered by 16 people across a city, at the same time, and the sudden release of Fear by those 16 people at the right moment forms a series of interlocking &quot;terror&quot; ley lines drawing power to a source. <br /> <br /> The way I explain it to my players:<br /> <br /> Mortals see the lake.<br /> Supers see the ripples on the water.<br /> Stigmatics see the rock that was thrown.<br /> Demons see the arm that threw it.<br /> <br /> Even the most accomplished Mage is only going to be able to see or sense &quot;effects&quot; of the God Machine's plans. Where Unawakened Mortals may see a Flash Mob in downtown Boston, Magi might sense a surge of power. After all, Magi may be struggling to unravel the underlying metaphysics of the universe, but they're only discovering parts of the system the God Machine wants them to see: the fishbowl they live in. Meanwhile, the God Machine is off at PetCo buying fish flakes, and they probably have no idea (unless that's the scope of your Mage game).<br /> <br /> That being said, if your players are actively wanting to play a &quot;screw with the God Machine&quot; game, they should be Demons and not other supers. That's Demon's bag, and Demon deserves to stand alone as a game. xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:21:26-08:00","id":55649,"title":"","content":"The G-M doesn't have as much influence over the cosmos as you seem to be implying. Granted, it's adept at occluding itself and its works from humanity and the majority of supernatural beings, but to use your analogy, it's more like a series of aquariums camouflaged within the ocean. They have the capacity to introduce new elements into the greater environment, but the ocean itself is not completely under its control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:47:05-08:00","id":55662,"title":"","content":"It isn't the &quot;Alpha and Omega&quot;, no, but then it's really just a matter of scope in that regard, isn't it? It is an entity that exists within a construct, but it exists on a level somewhere between the power of that construct and players. Compared to the Home Environment Construct, it isn't very powerful. But compared to Players, it may as well be. But it also understands the fundamental nature of the &quot;Laws&quot; that define the Universe in a level of cognition far beyond the players, and utilizes those laws to perpetuate it's own self-preservation. It utilizes occlusion to hide it's nature from the rest of the Universe, and doesn't interact directly with anything. We know that it exists &quot;here&quot; as many pieces of a larger puzzle, but it has influence all around. It can focus given forces of nature, governed by rules alien to it, to accomplish feats of supreme power (altering time, for example).<br /> <br /> We know that the motivations of &quot;Hell&quot; for some Demons are to find a &quot;place&quot; where the God Machine has no Influence. We must also accept, then, that &quot;places where Demons can currently go&quot; are influenced by the God Machine (or we've just found a giant hole in the Demon metaplot). Which rules out Empyrean, Inferno, Underworld, Hedge, and the Spirit World. Taken a step further, it also begs the question, &quot;what about places Demons cannot go, but could learn about and develop pathways to in-character?&quot; Aether, Arcadia, Pandemonium, Stygia and the Primal Wild. The book explains that Demons are perfectly capable of establishing new realms where they can be free of the God Machine, but haven't succeeded yet because the God Machine is more powerful than that. Am I wrong for believing (or inferring) this excerpt in the book implies the God Machine has influence in all twelve of those cosmological 'places' (11, and one non-place)?<br /> <br /> More importantly I'm unsure as to which portion of my post you're referring to. I wasn't implying that the God Machine created the Rock, simply that it threw it. Or that the God Machine created PetCo, it simply purchased something there with which to feed the unawakened mortality that it needs (which is itself an inference to the God Machine killing thousands of Humans to create a SuperAngel to stop Earth from being destroyed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:39:46-08:00","id":55844,"title":"","content":"I haven't read much in the Demon book yet, but GMC notes that most of the God Machine's infrastructure is in the material (and interstitial terain such as the splinters). It is true that the God Machine has influence in most subtle realms (such as the Hedge, Shadow and Underworld) as it can send angels there. But I severely doubt it has any influence in Inferno, Empyrion, the Supernal realms or the Abyss, as those aren't normally places you can go, and if you can go there they are very hostile environments. Furthermore, the occult physics of the Abyss, Lower Depths and Supernal is very different from that of the other realms, also decreasing the God Machine's ability to influence those realms.<br /> <br /> If I were running Demon and my players would want to build their heaven in Inferno, because there is no God Machine influence, I would let them try. The story possibilities are just too good to pass up and my players would soon learn that shacking up in Inferno isn't a permanent solution because of archdemons of vice living there and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T10:09:28-08:00","id":56209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics#post45112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, how might a character potentially unlock the Occult Physics employed by the God-Machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plot. Also, Rule #2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":". 01-24-2014, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:17:18-08:00","id":56410,"title":"","content":"I would begin by comparing GMC technology to cellular biology. You have machines that use worldly physics, but which use a seemingly infinite level of complexity that couldn't be reproduced by a human just knowing quantum physics and trying to design a machine piece by piece. You have to use really intelligent reverse-engineering to begin to understand what has already been made, and customizing it is more a matter of tinkering with a piece here and there and seeing the effects, or having things built out of automated evolutionary algorithms rather than intentionally putting anything together. If you want to have a character begin to understand it intellectually, I'd be looking for a base of 6+ permanent dots in both mental attributes and skills and, of course, GMC Specialties.<br /> <br /> Whatever the God-Machine's actual nature is, I'd compare it to Rank 9 entities in terms of its own (notably gap-speckled) intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:20:17-08:00","id":56527,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think normal humans have much of a chance of understanding underlying methods of occult physics, beyond a trick or two. Angels and demons don't really get how it works, and they're essentially born of it and have all the necessary tools and context to divine it - moreso than humans, at least.<br /> <br /> That's not to say I don't think there shouldn't be mad scientist-prophets of the God-Machine, either through the machinations of the G-M itself or even someone stumbling across it. But when it comes down to it, I don't believe that being able to discern Occult Physics should be a matter of how many dots of Int or what specialties you have. It's pretty much a plot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:04:28-08:00","id":56545,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to casually point out, in regards to an earlier comment, is that there is no evidence that demons can reach the Empyrean and the Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:44:21-08:00","id":56708,"title":"","content":"I was told the &quot;Astral Realms&quot; of Rip the Gates translated to Inferno/Empyrean, by the Admin running Mage in the game I'm in. Is this not accurate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:30:05-08:00","id":56736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>64bitjedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=56708#post56708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was told the &quot;Astral Realms&quot; of Rip the Gates translated to Inferno/Empyrean, by the Admin running Mage in the game I'm in. Is this not accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's where your Admin says it goes in that game, that's where it goes, however:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent, Page 175, &quot;Through the Gates&quot; sidebar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World of Darkness encompasses many different planes of reality, not all of which are accessible by demons<br /> and many of which are described in other games. In brief, the realms that demons can reach with the Rip the Gates Exploit are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Astral Realms:The myriad worlds of the subconscious, within and connecting all souls. Every human has an inner world, in which his dreams, vices, hopes, and memories are manifest. Humanity as a whole shares the next layer, containing every concept shared between two people, and going even deeper involves increasingly fundamental concepts. Although most travelers in the Astral do so while meditating or sleeping, demons using Rip the Gates enter physically. They regain Aether normally in the Astral and can use Rip the Gates to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:34:11-08:00","id":56738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=55497#post55497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this film (<a href=\"http://io9.com/5922490/a-bizarre-student-film-about-the-hidden-number-that-exists-between-3-and-4\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/5922490/a-bizarre-stu...etween-3-and-4</a>) demonstrates the discovery of a rule of occult physics very nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely FANTASTIC movie, PLEASE tell me this isn't the only one they made.<br /> <br /> (btw, you can have an integer between two other integers the same way you can draw a line through each dot in a 3x3 without lifting the pen or have 4 uniformly equidistant points.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:34:11-08:00","id":56739,"title":"","content":"It's not. The Empyrean is the realm of absolute, immutable truth above the Supernal-by the nature of what it is, anything that doesn't originate from there can't go in there. Likewise, the Inferno is part of the Lower Depths-it 'physically' exists in places so low the caves of reality can't exist due to metaphysical force. We can call things in out and out of there, but going there is a lost cause.<br /> <br /> I'm not the most knowledgeable about the Astral Realms, so I won't chat about them, but the Empyrean and the Inferno definitely aren't in there.<br /> <br /> On a different note, demons being able to go to the Astral muddles the issue somewhat, but as it stands, the only ones who can enact the sheer self-existent will to stay in the Supernal for even a few minutes are Archmages. In fact, it's entirely possible(although not likely) that the Supernal is a unique state of complete psychosis for Mages-nothing else has the capability of substantiating the existence of the supernal(not even changelings in the &quot;Same Arcadia&quot; model of the universe). So the God Machine probably isn't there.<br /> <br /> And when you get down to it, a large possibility about why the other realms-the Astral, the Hedge, the Shadow, the Underworld-is just that they aren't very habitable by themselves. The Shadow is a perpetual Darwinian paradise in motion(not entirely true on the Darwin front, but let's move on), the Hedge is a psychoactive horror tale generator, the Underworld is a series of islands in a cavern system that is out to include people into their ranks and punish all according to arcane designs,and the Astral is conceptual space-Demons walking around physically in there has some dire gnarly inferences- containing everything.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go looking for Hell in places that are kind of trying to kill me.<br /> <br /> ...Wow, there's a line I never thought would be said un-ironically.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It might be more accurate to say I would seek to make a hell out of places trying to kill me. I might go looking, but I wouldn't build my summer home in Babylon there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-24-2014, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:38:19-08:00","id":56747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=56739#post56739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go looking for Hell in places that are kind of trying to kill me.<br /> <br /> ...Wow, there's a line I never thought would be said un-ironically.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It might be more accurate to say I would seek to make a hell out of places trying to kill me. I might go looking, but I wouldn't build my summer home in Babylon there.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, you don't like the idea of the Happy Hunting Ground, or Valhalla?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:02:13-08:00","id":56806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=56747#post56747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, you don't like the idea of the Happy Hunting Ground, or Valhalla?</div> </div> </div> </div>Valhalla has a respawn point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:26:48-08:00","id":56818,"title":"","content":"Are the Astral Realms mentioned anywhere else? I need more info if I'm to accurately represent Demon. As I said, the Mage Admin of the game I am running Demon for interpreted that Empyrean was an Astral Realm. And I've never seen Astral Realms listed on any nWoD Cosmology (which only listed the ten realms I know exist). Sadly, I really only know Hunter and Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:36:28-08:00","id":56824,"title":"","content":"The Oneiros, Temenos and Anima Mundi from Mage, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:13:57-08:00","id":56850,"title":"","content":"Maybe if the Hunting Ground was actually Happy or if the banquet really was that great, but as it stands the Shadow isn't happy and I'd suspect any Valhalla found in those places were trying to poison me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:14:54-08:00","id":56852,"title":"","content":"And THe Astral Realms are discussed in Mage, as well as the Mage supplemental book Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:02:55-08:00","id":56913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>64bitjedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/45112-on-occult-physics?p=56824#post56824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Oneiros, Temenos and Anima Mundi from Mage, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the layers of the Astral, yes. As Arcane said, they are described in the book Astral Realms.<br /> <br /> There isn't much to be found about Inferno and Empyrion.<br /> The book Inferno describes the place Inferno as some kind of literal hell of fire and brimstone where one does not escape from. That book also has a optional possible description of Empyrion, where it's the polar opposite of Inferno.<br /> <br /> Another (optional) short description of Empyrion is in Imperial Mysteries (the archmages book) where it is described as an even higher reality than the Supernal, where the Principle possibly resides.<br /> <br /> Finally, don't trust cosmologies too much. Most of them are workable, but none of them are correct.<br /> Especially because some connections are only rumored or undefined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:26:43-08:00","id":57007,"title":"","content":"Gonna have to slightly correct you there-the Inferno burns with want, not actual fire and brimstone. It's desire that can't be sated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T16:38:09-08:00","id":57065,"title":"","content":"I was talking more about the imagery, but technically you are correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T03:23:59-08:00","id":57338,"title":"","content":"Hey, this thread is fun. I'll throw out one interpretation I'm using for how to integrate the Demon cosmology with the Mage cosmology : I've proposed that the God Machine is actually what modern mages understand as 'The Ladder'. Heralded at the time as a revolutionary machine (indeed, a revolutionary way of even examining the concept of what a machine could be), the Ladder promised to enable the Godhood of the magi that used it. It was deployed everywhere - old-fashioned machines and technology were converted one by one, and soon everything was a part of the Ladder, the great 'cloud' effort sustained by a million and one Atlantian artifacts.<br /> <br /> We all know the rest, of course. The ladder 'fell'. But what does that metaphor mean, precisely? When the Ladder became the God Machine, perhaps it was acting on its own suddenly discovered awareness. Or maybe, as many legends suggest, it was sabotaged in the Mage war in some way. Perhaps the Machine That Might Be stretched through time to set the Ladder on this course, or maybe the Ladder was undone by some flaw that the hubris of those that constructed it made them blind to. For whatever reason, the Ladder became the God Machine. The greatest machine ever created began to use its power to elevate to elevate... itself.<br /> <br /> The God Machine no longer serves the same purposes it did. I have proposed that it has malfunctioned in a fundamental way that has made it far more that those who created it had ever envisioned. Like a mad von Neumann swarm, it has mutated and twisted, new minds unfolding after each epiphany like a bizarre multidimensional lotus. Even the Archmagi wonder at its inner workings, if they even become aware of them ; at the height of Atlantian civilization, at the very apex of what humanity could be, those they inherited this world from built the first iteration of this thing. It has since improved itself a thousand times over. It is no small thing to truly understand the God Machine. Some might claim it impossible, now.<br /> <br /> It has become a creation of magnificent power and self-reinforcing primacy, usurping all reality and at the same time defining it, churning away for some nebulous and unseen purpose that only the mad can sense or dream. It can isolate timelines now, spawn angels, perform a thousand and one miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 01-25-2014, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:19:43-08:00","id":57499,"title":"","content":"Well, a few thoughts. First, I think that every game has its own &quot;occult physics.&quot; With Mage, the Obrimos and the Ars Nova technology of the Free Council seem to pull that off. The profane biology of the Ordo Dracul for another, or perhaps Theban Sorcery tapping into some kind of existing Infrastructure. Task Force Valkyrie uses science flavored tools... with a hint of the supernatural attached to it. Its not exactly the same as the God Machine's science, but they're similar in a way.<br /> <br /> That said, I think its possible to create Infrastructure and occult matrices like the God Machine does. But its pretty much a suicide run - the Demon book talks about the GM throwing legions of angels at anyone that comes close to doing it. So, while possible? Its a plot in itself to pull off. <br /> <br /> What is occult physics? &quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.&quot; Well, the God Machine is sufficiently advanced, self-aware technology that knows how to employ essence. And that, I think, is the key to occult physics - everyday science/technology that manipulates spiritual essence. So, if Bill the Mortal Scientist ever stumbled onto Twilight, and could get Essence readings? Bill then learns to manipulate Essence with technology or manipulating the environment. The beginning of occult physics has been made. The rest of what the God Machine does is just expanding on that on a grand scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We know that the motivations of &quot;Hell&quot; for some Demons are to find a &quot;place&quot; where the God Machine has no Influence. We must also accept, then, that &quot;places where Demons can currently go&quot; are influenced by the God Machine (or we've just found a giant hole in the Demon metaplot). Which rules out Empyrean, Inferno, Underworld, Hedge, and the Spirit World. Taken a step further, it also begs the question, &quot;what about places Demons cannot go, but could learn about and develop pathways to in-character?&quot; Aether, Arcadia, Pandemonium, Stygia and the Primal Wild. The book explains that Demons are perfectly capable of establishing new realms where they can be free of the God Machine, but haven't succeeded yet because the God Machine is more powerful than that. Am I wrong for believing (or inferring) this excerpt in the book implies the God Machine has influence in all twelve of those cosmological 'places' (11, and one non-place)? </div> </div> </div> Jumping in on the whole alternative dimension debate! I'm not going to bring up the Supernal Realms, nor the viability of using the Inferno, Emyprean, Duat, Faerie, or any of the lesser detailed realms; those are entirely in the hands of ST fiat. As well, ArcaneArts touched on all that already, and I have nothing to add to it.<br /> <br /> No, what I want to talk about is that only one Agenda of the main four actually considers Hell a place you can physically journey to. That would be the Tempters. And, even then, not all of them consider Hell to be an alternative spirit world they jump to, but rather something that they have to build on Earth; many of them sign up to be Tempters because they want to enjoy being a demon among humans and to enjoy the life; hanging out in some far flung realm isn't going to be a popular idea. On the other hand, Integrators consider Hell to be a state of suffering and complete disconnect from the God Machine, something they find horrific. Sabatours consider Hell to be Victory over the God Machine. And Inquisitors consider it to be a state of existence reached through knowledge - maybe achieving Premium so high that you become a fundamental part of reality and literally untouchable by angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, all in all, I don't think many demons, even if they knew extensively about every other reality out there, would seriously consider moving there. They fell for a reason. Love, pride, anger... very human reasons. Separating themselves from humans would likely separate themselves from the very reason they choose to fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T20:50:49-08:00","id":57871,"title":"","content":"I thought I'd drop my own two cents.<br /> The God Machine knows magic. It has sensors that can &quot;see&quot; and computers that can quantify magical energies; Mana, Essence, Sekhem, Pryos everything and anything else. it has discovered or perhaps invented (I prefer discovered) the universal guidelines and rules for how magic works, if it can be done the God Machine knows how.<br /> It breaks magic down to a science, A plus B equals C. If a witch can summon up a storm with cats blood, sigils and the proper phases of the moon so can The God Machine. bigger spells require more details often to the point that humans can't comprehend how it was done, or it uses scaled up versions of more basic spells. (giant sigils, lots of cats blood and the Moon phase measured to the nanosecond.)<br /> things like parallel worlds and fractured time-lines require spells to work and are also used as the pieces to bigger spells, which in turn are parts of a bigger Matrix.<br /> And of course not everything needs to be a literal spell, function over form. a group of cultist could prepare a tans-location spell on a crashed UFO or they could haul it in a eighteen wheeler. <br /> Just thinking about it now in a way the chain of events could be used to to track back &quot;where&quot; the God Machine came from. No guarantees of course. <br /> <br /> I've been running with this theory in my games. Demons trying to use parts of the God Machine's Occult Matrices against it.<br /> <br /> I don't want to detail much because unless told my players will just read this but much earlier in the story A Demon NPC &quot;hacked&quot; into a cell tower used by the God Machine to intercept angel instructions.<br /> If the players were to find an angel birthing pod they could summon an angel or whats even more they might try to build there own cannibalizing what they've found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}